      "part_type": "Hadith",
      "path": "/books/al-kafi:6:6:2:5",
      "text": [
        " سَأَلْتُهُ عَنْ أَكْلِ الضَّبِّ فَقَالَ إِنَّ الضَّبَّ وَ الْفَأْرَةَ وَ الْقِرَدَةَ وَ الْخَنَازِيرَ مُسُوخٌ ."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.hubeali": [
          "Ali Bin Ibrahim, from his father, from Ibn Abu Umeyr, from Hammad, from Al Halby, ",
          "(It has been narrated) from Abu Abdullah<sup>asws</sup>, said, ‘I asked him<sup>asws</sup> about eating the lizard. So he<sup>asws</sup> said: ‘The lizard, and the mouse, and the monkey, and the pigs, are morphed (creatures)’."
        ],
        "en.sarwar": [
          "5. Ali ibn Ibrahim has narrated from his father from ibn abu ‘Umayr from Hammad from al-Halabiy who has said the following: “I once asked abu ‘Abd Allah, ‘Alayhi al-Salam, about eating lizards. He (the Imam) said, ‘Lizards, rats, apes and pigs are metamorphosed.’” "
        ]
      }
    },
